{
  "$comment": "GENERATED, unlike its m3 sibling — captured verbatim from the `design-artifacts/remote-m3` delivery branch of yschimke/remote-m3-catalog-out at 52ed103, which `composePreviewDiscover` wrote from yschimke/remote-m3-catalog 4f6f808d (remote-m3 moved out of wear-m3-catalog into its own repository). remote-m3-record-v1.json is the same branch's `components.json`. That is the pair the cutover actually uses, so this fixture answers the question the hand-built m3 one cannot: can the catalog produce a usable published file. Regenerate the same way — take the delivery branch's `ui-builder.json` and re-add this key — whenever remote-catalog gains or loses a component, or its policy changes what a component declares.\n\n27 record components and a 26-entry menu, plus three builtins (the Small, Large and experimental Adaptive widget containers). The record and the menu differ by the one component the catalog EXCLUDES: `remote-m3/remote-sticker`, its own preview frame, which stays in the record carrying its `excluded` reason — that is what the schema means by \"kept off the shelf, with the stated reason\". The capture wrapper that used to be the second exclusion is gone from the record altogether: the catalog now uses the released `CapturingWearWidgetPreview` rather than its own copy.\n\nRe-capture after a republish rather than trusting a green run against a stale fixture: against an earlier capture the equivalence gate once scored 0/0/0/0 while the LIVE document had an unreviewed field.",
