        "propertyCapabilities": [
          {
            "name": "text",
            "jsonType": "string",
            "required": true,
            "notes": "The string the component draws. `RemoteText` takes a `RemoteString`, so a design's plain string is written as `\"…\".rs` and a binding or a state value as the remote expression it names — what the design carries is the same JSON either way."
          },
          {
            "name": "style",
            "jsonType": "string",
            "required": false,
            "allowedValues": [
              "displayLarge",
              "displayMedium",
              "displaySmall",
              "titleLarge",
              "titleMedium",
              "titleSmall",
              "labelLarge",
              "labelMedium",
              "labelSmall",
              "bodyLarge",
              "bodyMedium",
              "bodySmall",
              "bodyExtraSmall",
              "numeralExtraLarge",
              "numeralLarge",
              "numeralMedium",
              "numeralSmall",
              "numeralExtraSmall"
            ],
            "notes": "A role on this catalog's type scale, written as `style = RemoteMaterialTheme.typography.<role>`. This is the way to set type here: a role carries size, weight, line height and letter spacing together through `RemoteTextStyle`, which is why the catalog's own stickers pass a role OR an explicit size and never both. The eighteen are `RemoteTypography`'s own and are NOT the Material 3 fifteen — there is no `headline` on a watch, and there are five `numeral` roles a time or a metric is set in. A role this class does not have would export as a call that does not compile, so the list is exactly what it publishes."
          },
          {
            "name": "fontSize",
            "jsonType": "number",
            "required": false,
            "notes": "Size in sp, as an override on top of `style` rather than a substitute for it — set it alone and everything else about the type comes from the ambient style. Spelled the parameter's own way; a design authored against the borrowed `m3/text` says `fontSizeSp` and the writer reads both. A whole number writes `22.rsp`; a fractional one writes `14.5f.sp.asRemoteTextUnit()`, because `RemoteTextUnitKt` publishes no `Float.rsp`."
          },
          {
            "name": "color",
            "jsonType": "string",
            "required": false,
            "notes": "A colour: a `#RRGGBB` literal, which exports as `Color(0x…).rc`, or one of `colorTokens.roles`, which exports as `RemoteMaterialTheme.colorScheme.<role>`."
          },
          {
            "name": "textAlign",
            "jsonType": "string",
            "required": false,
            "allowedValues": [
              "start",
              "center",
              "end",
              "justify"
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "maxLines",
            "jsonType": "integer",
            "required": false
          }
        ],
